---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="A binary min-heap and its rivals, with every comparison counted (a step is one element examined), never timed. All inputs come from fixed formulas, so the numbers never change. Large sizes take a moment: some of the slow variants really do tens of millions of steps.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Set <b>Items n</b> to <b>10,000</b>. In <b>Building a heap</b>, pushing items one at a time costs <b>22,831</b> comparisons on random input and <b>113,631</b> on descending input (each new item is the smallest so far and climbs to the top), while bottom-up heapify costs <b>18,779</b> and <b>19,982</b>: about two comparisons per item whatever the order.</li>
    <li>In <b>The top k</b>, set <b>Top k</b> to <b>10</b>: a heap of 10 needs <b>10,285</b> comparisons on random input against <b>120,463</b> to sort everything. Set <b>Top k</b> to <b>100</b>: <b>14,733</b> on random input, but <b>123,566</b> on ascending input (every new item beats the smallest kept one), which is more than the full sort.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Items n</b> to <b>1,000</b>. In <b>Three ways to store a priority queue</b>: an unsorted array needs <b>501,500</b> steps for n pushes and n pops, a sorted array <b>246,079</b> and a heap <b>17,194</b>. In <b>Decrease-key</b>, a heap that knows where each item sits needs <b>17,707</b> comparisons in all, one that scans for the item <b>684,633</b> steps, and lazy duplicates <b>37,818</b> (the heap grows to <b>2,000</b> entries).</li>
    <li>In <b>A scheduler that starves a task</b>, set <b>Aging</b> to <b>No aging</b>: the priority-9 task from tick 0 never runs within 2000 ticks. Set <b>Aging</b> to <b>One priority level = 10 ticks</b>: it is served at tick <b>43</b>.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg hp" data-hp>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Items n <select class="pg-in" data-n><option value="10">10</option><option value="100">100</option><option value="1000">1,000</option><option value="10000" selected>10,000</option></select></label>
      <label>Top k <select class="pg-in" data-k><option value="10" selected>10</option><option value="100">100</option><option value="half">Half of n</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Building a heap</h3>
      <div class="pg-grid">
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)"><h3>n pushes, random input</h3><span class="pg-mono hp-big" data-bp1></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--good)"><h3>Bottom-up heapify, random input</h3><span class="pg-mono hp-big" data-bp2></span><span class="pg-note" data-bp2n></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" data-bpb3><h3>n pushes, descending input</h3><span class="pg-mono hp-big" data-bp3></span><span class="pg-note">each new item is the smallest so far and climbs to the root</span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--good)"><h3>Bottom-up heapify, descending input</h3><span class="pg-mono hp-big" data-bp4></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>The top k</h3>
      <div class="pg-grid">
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--good)"><h3>Heap of k, random input</h3><span class="pg-mono hp-big" data-tk1></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" data-tkb2><h3>Heap of k, ascending input</h3><span class="pg-mono hp-big" data-tk2></span><span class="pg-note" data-tk2n></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)"><h3>Sort everything (merge sort)</h3><span class="pg-mono hp-big" data-tk3></span><span class="pg-note" data-tk3n></span></div>
      </div>
      <span class="pg-note" data-tkv></span>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Three ways to store a priority queue</h3>
      <div class="pg-grid">
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--bad)"><h3>Unsorted array</h3><span class="pg-mono hp-big" data-pq1></span><span class="pg-note">push is free, every pop scans all items</span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--bad)"><h3>Array kept sorted</h3><span class="pg-mono hp-big" data-pq2></span><span class="pg-note">pop is free, every push shifts items</span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--good)"><h3>Binary heap</h3><span class="pg-mono hp-big" data-pq3></span><span class="pg-note" data-pq3n></span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hp-bars" data-bars></div>
      <span class="pg-note" data-pqv></span>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Decrease-key</h3>
      <p class="pg-note">Every one of the n items gets a lower priority once, then the queue is drained. Totals are comparisons, plus the steps spent scanning in the second variant.</p>
      <div class="pg-grid">
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--good)"><h3>Heap knows each item's position</h3><span class="pg-mono hp-big" data-dk1></span><span class="pg-note" data-dk1n></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--bad)"><h3>Scan the array to find it</h3><span class="pg-mono hp-big" data-dk2></span><span class="pg-note" data-dk2n></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)"><h3>Lazy duplicates</h3><span class="pg-mono hp-big" data-dk3></span><span class="pg-note" data-dk3n></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>A scheduler that starves a task</h3>
      <div class="pg-row"><label>Aging <select class="pg-in" data-age><option value="1000000" selected>No aging</option><option value="100">One priority level = 100 ticks</option><option value="50">One priority level = 50 ticks</option><option value="10">One priority level = 10 ticks</option></select></label></div>
      <p class="pg-note">One task per tick arrives with priority 1 to 5 and one task is served per tick, most urgent first. A priority-9 task has been waiting since tick 0. The queue key is priority x ticks-per-level + arrival tick.</p>
      <div class="pg-box" data-sc style="--c: var(--border)"><h3>The priority-9 task</h3><span class="pg-mono hp-big" data-sc1></span><span class="pg-note" data-sc2></span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, formatThousands } from '../playground';

  // The same model as the code samples, ported to TypeScript.
  const ID_SPACE = 100000;
  function makeInput(pattern: string, n: number): number[] {
    const a: number[] = []; let x = 12345;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      x = (x * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296;
      const r = Math.floor(x / 65536) % 100000;
      a.push(pattern === 'descending' ? n - i : pattern === 'ascending' ? i + 1 : r);
    }
    return a;
  }
  class Heap {
    a: number[] = []; c = 0; pos: number[] | null;
    constructor(track = 0) { this.pos = track ? new Array(track).fill(0) : null; }
    put(i: number, key: number) { this.a[i] = key; if (this.pos) this.pos[key % ID_SPACE] = i; }
    siftUp(i: number) {
      const key = this.a[i];
      while (i > 0) { const p = Math.floor((i - 1) / 2); this.c++; if (key < this.a[p]) { this.put(i, this.a[p]); i = p; } else break; }
      this.put(i, key);
    }
    siftDown(i: number) {
      const key = this.a[i], n = this.a.length;
      for (;;) {
        let s = 2 * i + 1;
        if (s >= n) break;
        if (s + 1 < n) { this.c++; if (this.a[s + 1] < this.a[s]) s++; }
        this.c++;
        if (this.a[s] < key) { this.put(i, this.a[s]); i = s; } else break;
      }
      this.put(i, key);
    }
    push(key: number) { this.a.push(key); this.siftUp(this.a.length - 1); }
    pop(): number {
      const top = this.a[0], last = this.a.pop()!;
      if (this.a.length > 0) { this.a[0] = last; this.siftDown(0); }
      return top;
    }
    heapify(items: number[]) {
      this.a = items.slice();
      if (this.pos) this.a.forEach((key, i) => { this.pos![key % ID_SPACE] = i; });
      for (let i = Math.floor(this.a.length / 2) - 1; i >= 0; i--) this.siftDown(i);
    }
  }
  function mergeSortCount(a: number[]): number {
    let count = 0;
    const sort = (v: number[]): number[] => {
      if (v.length < 2) return v;
      const left = sort(v.slice(0, Math.floor(v.length / 2))), right = sort(v.slice(Math.floor(v.length / 2)));
      const out: number[] = []; let i = 0, j = 0;
      while (i < left.length && j < right.length) { count++; if (right[j] < left[i]) out.push(right[j++]); else out.push(left[i++]); }
      return out.concat(left.slice(i), right.slice(j));
    };
    sort(a);
    return count;
  }
  const prio = (i: number) => 20000 + ((i * 7919) % 10007);
  const lowered = (i: number) => prio(i) - 1 - ((i * 4999) % 15000);

  function building(n: number) {
    const out: Record<string, number> = {};
    for (const pattern of ['random', 'descending']) {
      const a = makeInput(pattern, n);
      const h = new Heap(); for (const v of a) h.push(v);
      const g = new Heap(); g.heapify(a);
      out[`push-${pattern}`] = h.c; out[`heapify-${pattern}`] = g.c;
    }
    return out;
  }
  function topK(n: number, k: number) {
    const heapSteps = (pattern: string) => {
      const a = makeInput(pattern, n); const h = new Heap(); h.heapify(a.slice(0, k));
      for (const x of a.slice(k)) { h.c++; if (x > h.a[0]) { h.a[0] = x; h.siftDown(0); } }
      return h.c;
    };
    return { random: heapSteps('random'), ascending: heapSteps('ascending'), sort: mergeSortCount(makeInput('random', n)) };
  }
  function storage(n: number) {
    const a = makeInput('random', n);
    let u: number[] = [], stepsU = 0;
    for (const v of a) { u.push(v); stepsU++; }
    while (u.length > 0) {
      stepsU += u.length;
      let m = 0; for (let i = 1; i < u.length; i++) if (u[i] < u[m]) m = i;
      u[m] = u[u.length - 1]; u.pop(); // order is irrelevant to the count: every pop scans the whole array
    }
    const s: number[] = []; let stepsS = 0;
    for (const v of a) {
      s.push(v); let j = s.length - 1;
      while (j > 0) { stepsS++; if (s[j - 1] < v) { s[j] = s[j - 1]; j--; } else break; }
      s[j] = v;
    }
    while (s.length > 0) { s.pop(); stepsS++; }
    const h = new Heap(); for (const v of a) h.push(v); while (h.a.length > 0) h.pop();
    return { unsorted: stepsU, sorted: stepsS, heap: h.c };
  }
  function decreaseKey(n: number) {
    const start: number[] = []; for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) start.push(prio(i) * ID_SPACE + i);
    const h = new Heap(n); h.heapify(start); let base = h.c;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const j = h.pos![i]; h.a[j] = lowered(i) * ID_SPACE + i; h.siftUp(j); }
    const updA = h.c - base; while (h.a.length > 0) h.pop(); const totalA = h.c - base;
    const g = new Heap(); g.heapify(start); base = g.c; let scan = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { let j = 0; while (g.a[j] % ID_SPACE !== i) j++; scan += j + 1; g.a[j] = lowered(i) * ID_SPACE + i; g.siftUp(j); }
    while (g.a.length > 0) g.pop();
    const totalB = g.c - base + scan;
    const z = new Heap(); z.heapify(start); base = z.c;
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) z.push(lowered(i) * ID_SPACE + i);
    const peak = z.a.length; while (z.a.length > 0) z.pop();
    return { indexed: totalA, scan: totalB, scanSteps: scan, lazy: z.c - base, peak, updA };
  }
  function scheduler(age: number): number | null {
    const h = new Heap(); h.push((9 * age) * 10000);
    for (let t = 1; t <= 2000; t++) {
      const p = ((t * 7 + 3) % 5) + 1;
      h.push((p * age + t) * 10000 + t);
      if (h.pop() % 10000 === 0) return t;
    }
    return null;
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-hp]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const colour = (id: string, c: string) => q<HTMLElement>(id).style.setProperty('--c', c);
    const sel = (s: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(s).value;
    const cache = new Map<string, any>();
    const memo = <T,>(key: string, f: () => T): T => { if (!cache.has(key)) cache.set(key, f()); return cache.get(key); };
    function draw() {
      const n = Number(sel('[data-n]'));
      const b = memo(`b${n}`, () => building(n));
      q('[data-bp1]').textContent = formatThousands(b['push-random']);
      q('[data-bp2]').textContent = formatThousands(b['heapify-random']);
      q('[data-bp2n]').textContent = `${Math.round((b['heapify-random'] / n) * 100) / 100} per item: bounded by about 2n`;
      q('[data-bp3]').textContent = formatThousands(b['push-descending']);
      q('[data-bp4]').textContent = formatThousands(b['heapify-descending']);
      colour('[data-bpb3]', b['push-descending'] > 2 * b['heapify-descending'] ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--border)');

      const kWanted = sel('[data-k]') === 'half' ? Math.floor(n / 2) : Number(sel('[data-k]'));
      const k = Math.max(1, Math.min(kWanted, Math.floor(n / 2)));
      const t = memo(`t${n}/${k}`, () => topK(n, k));
      q('[data-tk1]').textContent = formatThousands(t.random);
      q('[data-tk2]').textContent = formatThousands(t.ascending);
      q('[data-tk2n]').textContent = 'every new item beats the smallest kept one, so each one sifts down';
      colour('[data-tkb2]', t.ascending > t.sort ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--border)');
      q('[data-tk3]').textContent = formatThousands(t.sort);
      q('[data-tk3n]').textContent = 'about n log2 n, on any input';
      q('[data-tkv]').textContent = `Effective k = ${formatThousands(k)} of ${formatThousands(n)} items. ${t.ascending > t.sort ? 'Here the heap on ascending input costs more than sorting everything: a heap of k only wins while k is small against n, and the worst input is one where every item enters.' : 'The heap costs about n log2 k, the sort about n log2 n: the gap shrinks as k grows.'} Getting the k items in order costs a further k log k.`;

      const p = memo(`p${n}`, () => storage(n));
      q('[data-pq1]').textContent = formatThousands(p.unsorted);
      q('[data-pq2]').textContent = formatThousands(p.sorted);
      q('[data-pq3]').textContent = formatThousands(p.heap);
      q('[data-pq3n]').textContent = `both push and pop cost about log2 n: ${Math.round(p.unsorted / p.heap)}x fewer than the unsorted array`;
      const bars = q('[data-bars]'); bars.textContent = '';
      const rows: [string, number][] = [['Unsorted array', p.unsorted], ['Sorted array', p.sorted], ['Binary heap', p.heap]];
      const top = Math.log10(Math.max(...rows.map((r) => r[1]), 10));
      for (const [label, v] of rows) {
        const row = document.createElement('div'); row.className = 'hp-bar';
        const name = document.createElement('span'); name.textContent = label;
        const track = document.createElement('span'); track.className = 'hp-track';
        const fill = document.createElement('span'); fill.className = 'hp-fill'; fill.style.width = `${Math.max(2, (Math.log10(Math.max(1, v)) / top) * 100)}%`;
        track.appendChild(fill);
        row.append(name, track); bars.appendChild(row);
      }
      q('[data-pqv]').textContent = `Bars are on a log scale. At one step per nanosecond (an assumption), the unsorted array's ${formatThousands(p.unsorted)} steps take ${p.unsorted / 1e9 < 0.001 ? 'under a millisecond' : `about ${Math.round(p.unsorted / 1e6)} milliseconds`}; the growth is what matters: quadratic against n log n.`;

      const d = memo(`d${n}`, () => decreaseKey(n));
      q('[data-dk1]').textContent = formatThousands(d.indexed);
      q('[data-dk1n]').textContent = `the updates alone cost ${formatThousands(d.updA)}: one sift-up each, at most log2 n levels`;
      q('[data-dk2]').textContent = formatThousands(d.scan);
      q('[data-dk2n]').textContent = `${formatThousands(d.scanSteps)} of them are the scans for the item`;
      q('[data-dk3]').textContent = formatThousands(d.lazy);
      q('[data-dk3n]').textContent = `no position index needed, but the heap grows to ${formatThousands(d.peak)} entries and ${formatThousands(n)} stale ones are popped and skipped`;

      const age = Number(sel('[data-age]'));
      const served = memo(`s${age}`, () => scheduler(age));
      q('[data-sc1]').textContent = served === null ? 'never within 2000 ticks' : `served at tick ${served}`;
      q('[data-sc2]').textContent = served === null ? 'every arrival is more urgent, so it waits forever: starvation' : `waiting ${served} ticks: a task gains one priority level for every ${age} ticks it waits`;
      colour('[data-sc]', served === null ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
    }
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .pg-mono { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .playground label { max-width: 100%; }
  .playground select.pg-in { max-width: 100%; }
  .playground .hp-big { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .playground .hp-bars { display: grid; gap: 6px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .playground .hp-bar { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 9.5rem 1fr; gap: 2px 8px; align-items: center; }
  .playground .hp-track { display: block; height: 12px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--surface-2); overflow: hidden; }
  .playground .hp-fill { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 6px; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .playground .hp-bar { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
